>I've burned through about 20 crystal ball charges (boy are they heavy) and
>haven't been able to get to the portal quickly enough.  How do find and
>get to it in time?

Couple points:

1) Remember, the portal's bubble is moving also.  It isn't good enough
to move to where it is *now*. You need to move to where it's *going to
be*.

2) Predicting the path of the bubble is not easy.   My suggestion would
be to wield or wear the amulet of Yendor.   The amulet will go from
"warm" to "very warm" to "hot" as it gets closer to the portal.  If you
can't see the portal when the amulet is hot, *then* is the time to take
a crystal ball or scroll look (you did know that a certain kind of
scroll will tell you where a trap is in one turn, right?).  This close,
you have a chance of running down the portal.

3). Or alternatively. Just find a bubble and stand still in it.
Eventually, the portal will come to YOU as the bubble it is in
eventually merges with your bubble.  Then just walk over.  I'm told
this will work, although I've never actually tried it.

